# gentoo-install — package set: desktop
# inherits: server
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# server, plus a graphical session that works before any desktop environment
# is installed: a display server, audio, fonts and a terminal.
#
# No desktop environment is listed, and that is deliberate. GNOME, Plasma,
# Xfce and the rest are a choice with a Portage profile attached
# (default/linux/amd64/23.0/desktop/plasma and friends, see data/profiles.tsv);
# an installer that picks one promotes its author's taste to a default
# (DESIGN.md §15). Select the profile, then emerge the meta-package.
#
# One atom per line, # starts a comment.

media-fonts/dejavu              # without a font, a graphical session shows empty boxes
media-fonts/noto                # the rest of the world's scripts
media-sound/pipewire            # audio and screen sharing, replacing pulseaudio and jack
media-video/wireplumber         # pipewire does nothing without a session manager
net-misc/networkmanager         # roaming between networks, which dhcpcd alone does not do
x11-apps/xrandr                 # the display is on the wrong output more often than not
x11-base/xorg-server            # Wayland compositors come with their DE; X is the floor
x11-misc/xdg-utils              # xdg-open, which half the applications shell out to
x11-terms/xterm                 # ugly, tiny, and it starts when nothing else will
